# Builder Rules

Project-specific instructions for Builder when working in this repo.

## Project

- App lives in `ecommerce/`. It's a Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS project.
- Package manager: npm (see `ecommerce/package.json` / `package-lock.json`).

## Design tokens

- The "Lulu" theme tokens (colors, fonts, type scale, spacing, radii) live in
  `ecommerce/src/lulu/tokens.ts` and are wired into `ecommerce/tailwind.config.ts`.
- Reuse existing tokens/utility classes instead of hardcoding new colors, font
  sizes, or one-off spacing values on `/lulu` pages.
- The Lulu spacing scale lines up 1:1 with Tailwind's default spacing scale,
  so plain utilities (`p-16`, `gap-6`, `mt-10`, etc.) already match it —
  no custom spacing classes needed.
- When applying visual-editor style changes (padding, margin, gap, etc.),
  never emit Tailwind arbitrary-value classes (e.g. `pt-[42px]`) for raw
  pixel diffs. Snap the value to the nearest step in `luluSpacing`
  (`ecommerce/src/lulu/tokens.ts`) and use the matching Tailwind utility
  instead of hardcoding the literal pixel value.

## Code style

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones.
- Do not add comments unless explaining a non-obvious "why".
- Do not add abstractions, error handling, or config options beyond what the
  task requires.
- Match existing formatting and naming conventions in the file being edited.

## Workflow

- Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, or create branches directly — the
  platform handles commits automatically and pushing/PRs go through the UI.
- Test UI changes in the live preview before considering a task done.
